event: content_block_start
data: {"type":"content_block_start","index":1,"content_block":{"type":"mcp_tool_result","tool_use_id":"mcptoolu_FIXTURE","is_error":false,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"jq is primarily written in C  . It is designed to be portable and has zero runtime dependencies .\n\n## Core Implementation Language\n\nThe core `jq` processor, which handles JSON parsing, filtering, and transformation, is implemented in C  . This includes its lexer, parser, compiler, and virtual machine .\n\n## Documentation Build System\n\nWhile the `jq` tool itself is in C, its website and documentation are built using a Python-based static site generator . This system uses Python scripts, Jinja2 templates, and YAML content files to produce the static HTML pages for jqlang.org .\n\n## Notes\n\nThe question specifically asks about the language `jq` is written in, referring to the command-line tool itself. The documentation build system, while part of the `jqlang/jq` repository, is a separate component written in Python for generating the website.\n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- [JQ Overview (jqlang/jq)](/wiki/jqlang/jq#1)\n- [Core Architecture (jqlang/jq)](/wiki/jqlang/jq#2)\n- [Website and Download Documentation (jqlang/jq)](/wiki/jqlang/jq#6.2)\n\nView this search on DeepWiki: https://deepwiki.com/search/what-language-is-jq-written-in_4e033d64-77d5-4394-be7b-aaec01fff65f\n"}]}      }

